

⭐ TIME CRYSTAL ANALYZER PLUGIN (Final Form)

A plugin that detects temporal periodicity in Θ and visualizes:

oscillation frequency

amplitude

stability

phase

crystal boundaries

crystal lifetime

It uses only the plugin contract:

init
onFrame
render
onDestroy

Everything else is internal.

⭐ 1. Plugin Identity

id: "time_crystal_analyzer"
name: "Time Crystal Analyzer"

This is how the viewer recognizes it.

⭐ 2. What the plugin does (in one line)

Analyze Θ over time → detect periodic structures → visualize them

This is a temporal microscope.

⭐ 3. Data it reads

From frameState:

theta.min, theta.max, theta.avg

optional Θ grid (theta_XXXX.bin)

time t

Ξ regime

organism list

From viewerContext:

playback time

viewport geometry

events

settings

It never modifies anything.

⭐ 4. Internal State (Minimal)

The plugin keeps a rolling buffer:

history = [
  { t, theta_avg },
  { t, theta_avg },
  ...
]

Used for:

frequency detection

amplitude tracking

stability scoring

Buffer length: ~2–4 seconds of data.

⭐ 5. Time Crystal Detection Logic (Stripped‑Down)

A time crystal exists if:

Θ oscillates

Oscillation is periodic

Period is stable

Minimal algorithm:

collect theta_avg over time
compute FFT or autocorrelation
detect dominant frequency
measure amplitude
measure stability (variance of period)

If stability > threshold → crystal detected.

⭐ 6. Visualization Layers

The plugin renders three things:

🔷 A. Oscillation Graph (HUD Panel)

A small graph in the corner:

x‑axis: time

y‑axis: Θ average

line: oscillation waveform

highlight: detected period

This is the oscillation signature.

🔷 B. Crystal Boundary Overlay (Viewport)

If a crystal is detected:

draw a soft pulsing ring around the region

color = gold

pulse frequency = oscillation frequency

thickness = amplitude

This makes the crystal visible in the time fabric.

🔷 C. Crystal Stats Panel (HUD)

Shows:

Time Crystal Detected
frequency: 12.4 Hz
amplitude: 0.18
stability: 0.92
phase: 0.33π
lifetime: 1.8 s

This is the scientific readout.

⭐ 7. Plugin Lifecycle

init(viewerContext)

allocate history buffer

subscribe to playback events

create canvas layer

onFrame(frameState)

append Θ to history

run detection

update stats

render(ctx)

draw oscillation graph

draw crystal boundary

draw stats panel

onDestroy()

cleanup

remove canvas

